WEBVTT

00:03.390 --> 00:05.520
Huh? Um...

00:05.520 --> 00:06.810
Sayo-san?

00:06.810 --> 00:10.360
I'd like you to let me crash here,
starting now.

00:15.260 --> 00:16.910
Nice to meet you, new housemates.

00:20.570 --> 00:22.210
Why <i>here</i>?

01:54.730 --> 01:57.550
I'll explain later.

01:58.170 --> 02:00.970
But should I, uh, introduce myself first?

02:00.970 --> 02:04.930
Huh? Oh, well... I guess?

02:04.990 --> 02:08.710
<b>Gaku Shinoyama                                                     Polka Shinoyama</b>

02:05.430 --> 02:08.230
<i>Not like I can admit I 
already know who she is.</i>

02:06.540 --> 02:08.710
<b>Shinoyama                    Suzuka Shinoyama                          Sayo Shinoyama                         Kazuki Shinoyama</b>

02:09.560 --> 02:11.650
My name's Sayo Shinoyama.

02:11.650 --> 02:14.360
I'm Polka's niece,
although I'm older than him.

02:14.360 --> 02:16.740
This is my attendant.

02:16.740 --> 02:20.230
Lei-kun is a butler in training, apparently.

02:20.230 --> 02:21.880
Why the qualifier?

02:21.880 --> 02:23.690
Because I only found out today.

02:23.690 --> 02:24.950
Excuse me?

02:24.950 --> 02:29.170
X-Xiaoyu Lei! It's a pleasure to meet you!

02:29.170 --> 02:34.130
I'm Takumi Kuruya. I guess you 
could say I'm Polka's coworker.

02:34.510 --> 02:35.800
And this is—

02:35.800 --> 02:38.090
Misaki-chan, right? We met this morning.

02:38.090 --> 02:39.770
It's a small world!

02:40.800 --> 02:43.890
So, Sayo-san, what brings you here?

02:50.750 --> 02:51.700
Sharks.

02:51.700 --> 02:52.810
Sharks?

02:53.670 --> 02:56.240
My sharks... burned up.

02:58.320 --> 03:00.410
Yes, they burned.

03:00.740 --> 03:04.860
Burned like that scene in the kitchen 
of a marine medical research lab.

03:04.860 --> 03:07.610
Didn't you just love that cook?

03:07.610 --> 03:08.660
Huh? What?

03:09.040 --> 03:13.380
Young Miss Sayo lost her 
bedroom in today's fire,

03:13.380 --> 03:17.930
along with her collection 
of shark memorabilia.

03:19.160 --> 03:21.970
Rozan-sama entrusted me 
with a message for you.

03:23.820 --> 03:26.010
<i>Hey, sorry about this.</i>

03:26.010 --> 03:28.830
<i>I'd love to have a nice 
long chat over the phone,</i>

03:28.830 --> 03:31.850
<i>but the police and firefighters 
want to grill me.</i>

03:32.370 --> 03:36.310
<i>Your room and Sayo's
were totally incinerated.</i>

03:36.310 --> 03:42.570
<i>So, sorry, but would you put Sayo 
and her boy bodyguard up for a bit?</i>

03:43.040 --> 03:46.110
<i>Well, that's my pretext, anyway.</i>

03:46.810 --> 03:53.500
<i>Having two of my people in that building 
will make things a lot more convenient.</i>

03:54.650 --> 03:56.460
<i>I can sense</i>

03:56.970 --> 03:59.920
<i>more people keeping watch on this building.</i>

03:59.920 --> 04:01.630
<i>And this boy...</i>

04:01.630 --> 04:02.910
End of message!

04:03.400 --> 04:06.350
<i>The Shinoyamas already know about this place,</i>

04:06.760 --> 04:11.560
<i>so Rozan-san decided to 
send in his own security.</i>

04:12.010 --> 04:17.270
<i>But what if Sayo-san was behind 
the attempt on Polka-kun's life?</i>

04:17.590 --> 04:20.810
Do you prefer <i>Beach Shark</i> or <i>Ice Jaws</i>?

04:20.810 --> 04:21.740
I love 'em both!

04:23.440 --> 04:26.850
<i>In that case, I suppose this will save time.</i>

04:37.840 --> 04:40.420
Morning. Nice day, huh?

04:40.740 --> 04:43.200
Um... Morning.

04:43.590 --> 04:48.780
Don't you feel so full of 
life on mornings like this?

04:48.780 --> 04:51.670
Huh? Yes, I suppose.

04:51.670 --> 04:53.810
I don't.

04:53.810 --> 04:55.230
Er...

04:56.480 --> 04:59.890
But I respect your opinion.

04:59.890 --> 05:01.180
Good night.

05:01.690 --> 05:04.170
She picked a hell of a way to start her day.

05:04.170 --> 05:05.280
Morning!

05:05.510 --> 05:09.750
I'm terribly sorry! The young 
miss is still in shock.

05:09.750 --> 05:13.170
She wishes to sulk in bed for a while.

05:13.170 --> 05:18.680
If you want to get me out of this sleeping bag,
bait your hook with shark merch.

05:20.370 --> 05:22.500
Hey, quit it with the attempts at extortion.

05:23.080 --> 05:26.820
I guess we'd better clean 
up an empty room for them.

05:26.820 --> 05:29.740
Let's buy them a mattress 
at Don Quijote, too.

05:29.740 --> 05:32.510
You can't sleep on the floor forever.

05:32.510 --> 05:37.610
As long as I've got my shark 
sleeping bag, I can sleep anywhere.

05:38.210 --> 05:41.360
And I can sleep standing up, 
so you needn't bother!

05:41.610 --> 05:43.660
We can't just ignore you.

05:43.660 --> 05:46.240
No, please do.

05:46.240 --> 05:50.070
I'll see to the young miss's needs.

05:53.200 --> 05:54.660
By the way,

05:54.660 --> 05:57.250
why are you Sayo's attendant?

05:57.250 --> 06:01.590
I was chosen because we have similar names.

06:01.400 --> 06:03.460
<b>Xiaoyu</b>

06:01.520 --> 06:03.460
<b>Sayo</b>

06:01.590 --> 06:03.460
Not exactly great credentials.

06:03.460 --> 06:09.360
In addition to guarding young Miss Sayo,
I am to assist you, Polka-sama.

06:09.360 --> 06:11.010
Oh, I see.

06:11.350 --> 06:13.680
Would you please tell me 
how things are at home?

06:13.680 --> 06:16.890
You needn't ask so deferentially, Polka-sama.

06:17.390 --> 06:21.940
The main Shinoyama residence is 
once again buzzing with police,

06:21.940 --> 06:25.360
so it may be best that you 
not return for some time.

06:26.750 --> 06:28.360
Oh, okay.

06:28.700 --> 06:32.490
Before you knew it, the arsonist was down 
for the count, so you turned him in?

06:32.720 --> 06:34.930
Hey, who are those people?

06:34.930 --> 06:37.020
Police officers, I believe.

06:37.020 --> 06:38.120
What?!

06:38.790 --> 06:41.000
There's no way that's true.

06:43.060 --> 06:47.590
Oh? I thought the questioning 
finished yesterday.

06:48.940 --> 06:50.800
Just who we wanted to see.

06:51.280 --> 06:53.400
We're from a slightly different department.

06:53.400 --> 06:56.390
I know it's a hassle, 
but please bear with us,

06:56.390 --> 06:58.200
Takeru Shinoyama-san.

07:00.290 --> 07:05.230
You believe that yesterday's arsonist 
may have been the Fire-Breathing Bug?

07:05.230 --> 07:08.210
Yes, it's a possibility.

07:08.650 --> 07:11.380
I find that hard to believe.

07:11.380 --> 07:15.430
But if you're right, then I suppose his death

07:15.430 --> 07:19.500
means that the Fire-Breathing Bug 
won't be committing any more crimes.

07:19.500 --> 07:22.740
Oh, no, I wouldn't go that far.

07:23.260 --> 07:28.450
But we need to review this case thoroughly 
if we want to get to the truth.

07:32.430 --> 07:35.990
The Fire-Breathing Bug has always been 
a thorn in Shinoyama Security's side.

07:35.990 --> 07:40.610
They've burned several of our clients' 
buildings, tarnishing our reputation.

07:41.300 --> 07:46.150
We've been anxiously wondering when 
the police would put them behind bars.

07:46.420 --> 07:49.490
Really? That hits a sore spot.

07:49.490 --> 07:54.840
Of course, an arrest wouldn't count 
for much if they escaped from prison.

07:56.180 --> 07:58.470
Now you're rubbing salt in the wound.

07:58.470 --> 08:01.010
Aren't you assigned to Shinjuku Precinct?

08:01.010 --> 08:03.960
Do you really have time to 
sit around here chatting?

08:04.330 --> 08:07.370
I believe Ten'a Sorimura, 
the Phantom Solitaire,

08:07.900 --> 08:11.670
operates primarily in your jurisdiction.

08:08.900 --> 08:11.670
<b>Catch me if you can!</b>

08:09.780 --> 08:11.670
Catch me if you can!

08:12.160 --> 08:15.410
Our stock price dropped when he 
kidnapped the prime minister.

08:15.410 --> 08:18.090
And that wasn't even <i>our</i> security.

08:19.240 --> 08:22.730
I hope you'll ensure that 
it doesn't fall further.

08:24.090 --> 08:27.790
Good hunting, officers.

08:30.900 --> 08:33.110
I'd say that pair behind him

08:33.500 --> 08:36.090
are probably killers.

08:36.090 --> 08:37.410
Seriously?

08:37.740 --> 08:39.620
Something about them gives it away.

08:39.620 --> 08:43.410
Especially the man.
He smells like one of my kind.

08:43.670 --> 08:44.820
What kind's that?

08:44.820 --> 08:49.630
People who think they can solve 
any problem with violence.

08:50.000 --> 08:54.340
So, what you might call "scumbags."

08:55.120 --> 08:57.430
That's not too reassuring.

08:57.660 --> 09:00.640
Call up Pop Tozawa and Yatsu.

09:00.640 --> 09:04.470
We might throw down with Shinoyamas, 
depending on how this plays out.

09:05.370 --> 09:07.400
Have you got a lead?

09:10.820 --> 09:15.780
He was dressed up, but I bet you 
recognize the guy on the far left.

09:16.090 --> 09:17.450
Is that...?

09:17.450 --> 09:21.140
His name's Polka Shinoyama, 
and he's Rozan's younger son.

09:21.140 --> 09:23.790
That makes him an heir 
to the Shinoyama legacy.

09:23.790 --> 09:28.530
He's not at home now, but I hear 
he was there for yesterday's fire.

09:28.530 --> 09:32.000
That kid's a Shinoyama?

09:32.000 --> 09:37.840
The girl in glasses with him left footprints 
at the scene of the human knots.

09:38.430 --> 09:43.850
And I've learned that the victims were 
at odds with part of the Shinoyama Group.

09:43.850 --> 09:49.790
<b>Lemmings</b>

09:44.370 --> 09:47.760
We've been dealing with one troublemaker 
after another for the past month.

09:47.760 --> 09:50.810
Is this Polka kid at the center of it?

09:49.790 --> 09:50.810
<b>Fire-Breathing Bug</b>

09:51.220 --> 09:53.650
Or is Takeru Shinoyama?

09:54.230 --> 09:56.610
Let's blow this case wide open.

09:57.210 --> 09:58.120
What do you say?

09:59.810 --> 10:02.160
Tsubaki Iwanome, is it?

10:02.160 --> 10:06.740
I hear he once teamed up with an inspector 
to ruffle feathers in the police force,

10:07.250 --> 10:10.260
and I doubt money or 
pressure will silence him.

10:10.890 --> 10:11.840
Want him gone?

10:13.050 --> 10:15.970
No, we'll leave him to his own devices

10:15.970 --> 10:20.110
and hope that he exposes 
Polka's secrets for us.

10:20.600 --> 10:21.760
Of course,

10:22.120 --> 10:26.410
my grandfather seems to be 
making moves of his own.

10:31.310 --> 10:34.570
So, you and Sayo-san will use this room.

10:34.790 --> 10:36.890
I'm sorry for making you carry things.

10:36.890 --> 10:38.490
Don't sweat it.

10:38.490 --> 10:41.580
Anyway, are you really gonna 
sleep in this cubbyhole?

10:41.580 --> 10:43.740
Yes! I'll be fine here!

10:44.180 --> 10:46.450
Thank you all so much.

10:46.780 --> 10:48.700
Bye, then. Night!

10:52.590 --> 10:55.850
The more the merrier, right?

10:56.670 --> 10:57.850
I suppose so.

11:27.430 --> 11:30.830
Seriously, Polka. What are 
we gonna do about those two?

11:30.830 --> 11:33.920
<i>Good question, since we start 
fortune telling again tomorrow.</i>

11:33.920 --> 11:35.870
<i>What should we tell them?</i>

11:44.900 --> 11:48.270
I don't know why His Lordship trusts you,

11:48.720 --> 11:50.640
but I'll expose your whole plot,

11:51.440 --> 11:53.620
you impostor Polka Shinoyama.

11:54.840 --> 11:56.650
What do you mean, Your Lordship?!

11:57.660 --> 11:59.530
Just what I said.

11:59.950 --> 12:03.390
Would you head over to Shinjuku with Sayo?

12:08.930 --> 12:13.330
I understand, Your Lordship! You want 
me to eliminate the Polka impostor!

12:13.540 --> 12:18.110
No, numskull, the opposite. 
You're a Shinoyama bodyguard now.

12:18.110 --> 12:20.300
You don't need to do dirty jobs.

12:21.200 --> 12:25.760
That Polka is a fake, but he's not our enemy.

12:25.760 --> 12:28.860
What do you mean? Is the real Polka alive?

12:29.260 --> 12:33.160
Oh, well... You could say he's all right.

12:33.160 --> 12:38.330
Anyway, I can't explain,
but I'll vouch for that boy.

12:39.180 --> 12:42.250
Keep Sayo and the fake Polka safe.

12:42.630 --> 12:45.200
I know you can do that, Xiaoyu.

12:46.740 --> 12:52.160
I guess I'll have to. Your Lordship's 
orders are absolute, after all.

12:52.160 --> 12:55.480
I mean, you can refuse if you don't like it.

12:55.480 --> 12:56.790
Oh, fine! I'll do it!

12:56.790 --> 12:59.770
Just relax and lie down, Your Lordship!

13:00.740 --> 13:07.220
This is my chance. I'll exterminate 
this pest creeping up on His Lordship.

13:07.560 --> 13:12.180
And the real Polka, too,
while I'm at it. If he's still alive.

13:12.590 --> 13:18.940
I've never accepted that 
weakling as His Lordship's son.

13:18.940 --> 13:25.860
I would be a much more useful son 
to Rozan-sama than Polka ever could.

13:30.120 --> 13:35.360
<i>I'm... not broken... yet.</i>

13:35.670 --> 13:37.710
He'll never work again.

13:38.140 --> 13:41.590
Running into Agakura on his 
first job was bad luck.

13:41.590 --> 13:45.950
I suppose we should be glad that 
he <i>only</i> lost all four limbs.

13:46.830 --> 13:49.510
Xiaoyu will serve as a ting-hu from now on.

13:50.570 --> 13:51.350
<i>It can't be!</i>

13:51.770 --> 13:55.950
<i>No, Dad! I can still work! I'm alive!</i>

13:55.950 --> 13:59.580
<i>No! It's not true! Help me, Dad!</i>

13:59.940 --> 14:01.850
<i>Stop! Stop! Help!</i>

14:01.850 --> 14:04.240
<i>I'll crush you! I'll kill 
you if you touch me!</i>

14:04.240 --> 14:06.510
<i>Die, die, die, die, die!</i>

14:06.510 --> 14:09.120
Hey, what's a ting-hu?

14:09.820 --> 14:13.400
Rozan-sama. I'm sorry you heard that.

14:13.400 --> 14:17.810
True to its name, a ting hu or "garden pot" is a 
type of vessel passed down in our clan.

14:17.810 --> 14:19.660
Some of the poisons we employ

14:19.660 --> 14:25.800
require fungi that grow only in 
the entrails of living children.

14:25.800 --> 14:28.410
Don't be barbaric.

14:28.410 --> 14:31.280
Is that any way to treat your own son?

14:31.850 --> 14:38.690
Respectfully, our clan are not people. 
Whatever our bonds, we are all tools.

14:38.690 --> 14:44.570
To show compassion for a broken tool 
would be to neglect our duties.

14:45.390 --> 14:51.280
This is for your own protection. 
Do not question it.

14:51.280 --> 14:52.570
I see.

14:52.570 --> 14:57.500
Well, if you insist he's a tool, 
then you won't mind if I buy him.

14:57.500 --> 14:58.160
<i>Huh?</i>

14:58.160 --> 14:59.300
What?

14:59.300 --> 15:03.340
It's a little late to say you 
"can't sell your precious family."

15:03.580 --> 15:08.560
He is worthless as one of our hands,
but he has value as a ting-hu.

15:08.990 --> 15:11.240
I can't give him up cheaply.

15:11.240 --> 15:14.820
Yeah, I'll make it worth your while.

15:15.210 --> 15:19.540
I'll give you priority access 
to my group's latest tech.

15:19.850 --> 15:24.090
That way, you won't need those 
bullshit poisons to make a living.

15:25.530 --> 15:28.570
<i>What is this guy trying to say?</i>

15:28.570 --> 15:31.070
Don't mistake me for a Good Samaritan.

15:31.070 --> 15:35.160
I just want a guinea pig 
for my latest prosthetics.

15:35.850 --> 15:40.290
And then... Well, that can wait 
until you're back on your feet.

15:41.360 --> 15:45.040
Maybe you can give my 
family someone to talk to.

15:45.920 --> 15:49.760
<i>Oh. How long has it been</i>

15:50.660 --> 15:52.340
<i>since someone smiled at me?</i>

15:57.490 --> 15:58.710
Your Lordship...

16:00.250 --> 16:03.350
The Shinoyamas aren't just rich.

16:03.350 --> 16:08.320
They're well-connected in both 
reputable and criminal society.

16:08.670 --> 16:12.780
I hear they even have ties to other 
groups of assassins like ours.

16:12.780 --> 16:18.920
Meaning that whoever hired us
to kill Polka wasn't a Shinoyama?

16:18.920 --> 16:25.330
If they've got hitmen on call, it'd be 
easier to have it done in-house. Bang!

16:25.540 --> 16:27.670
I wouldn't be so sure.

16:28.290 --> 16:33.010
If I were in the client's position, 
I would have used a third party, too.

16:33.280 --> 16:37.740
It would be one thing if the whole 
Shinoyama family hated Polka,

16:37.740 --> 16:42.100
but their patriarch, Rozan, dotes on his son.

16:42.520 --> 16:46.810
Asking the family assassins to kill 
him would be asking for betrayal.

16:46.810 --> 16:53.000
So, what kind of people are the 
Shinoyamas' pet assassins, anyway?

16:53.000 --> 16:54.240
Well,

16:54.240 --> 16:59.700
the Lei family has bases in Shanghai,
Hong Kong, and Yokohama.

17:00.140 --> 17:05.750
It's not a rare surname, but the Leis that 
the Shinoyamas work with are special.

17:06.020 --> 17:11.290
They're called Heilei, "Black Lightning," 
and they mix old and new methods.

17:11.710 --> 17:17.720
From ancient poisons to the 
Shinoyama Group's latest tech,

17:19.260 --> 17:20.980
and everything in between.

17:24.050 --> 17:26.280
<i>Why not stick to business as usual for now?</i>

17:26.660 --> 17:30.620
<i>You're right. Sayo-san should 
already know that I tell fortunes.</i>

17:31.230 --> 17:35.100
Yesterday, you mentioned the 
"Venomous Dragon of Destruction."

17:35.100 --> 17:36.990
What other dragons are there?

17:37.200 --> 17:43.370
Well, Malfy the Home-wrecker Dragon takes 
beautiful human forms to seduce royalty.

17:43.700 --> 17:46.230
Malfy was feared as a menace

17:46.230 --> 17:49.130
but fell in love with the 
general of the Dazzling Corps.

17:49.130 --> 17:53.000
I think they eloped together 
when the empire fell.

17:53.000 --> 17:56.010
Running off with a dragon? 
Talk about romantic!

17:56.310 --> 18:00.780
There's also Goronzon the Vapor Dragon, 
Marm the Round Blade Dragon, and so on.

18:02.010 --> 18:04.840
<i>Dragon parts sell for high prices.</i>

18:04.840 --> 18:08.070
<i>And to make a dragon zombie, 
you need to buy one whole.</i>

18:08.070 --> 18:11.440
<i>He never shuts up about this 
video game or manga or whatever!</i>

18:11.440 --> 18:13.380
<i>Maybe a light novel?!</i>

18:13.380 --> 18:15.800
<i>What's wrong with him?!
Is he still in junior high?!</i>

18:17.080 --> 18:19.640
<i>And what's this rattling 
noise I keep hearing?</i>

18:20.000 --> 18:22.850
<i>It sounds like a bunch of dancing skeletons.</i>

18:22.950 --> 18:24.080
Yay! Yay!

18:24.080 --> 18:25.990
Isn't that a waste of magic?

18:24.410 --> 18:25.990
Yay! Yay!

18:25.990 --> 18:28.950
Yay! Yay!

18:26.150 --> 18:28.540
This doesn't take much.

18:29.470 --> 18:31.240
<i>Are they playing video games?!</i>

18:31.240 --> 18:33.000
<i>It doesn't really sound like it, though.</i>

18:33.000 --> 18:35.460
Hmm... If only we could quantify your mana reserves and consumption like in a video game.

18:33.980 --> 18:35.460
<i>I can hear them writing something.</i>

18:36.110 --> 18:40.430
<i>Maybe a tabletop RPG?
Is that rattling noise the dice?</i>

18:40.430 --> 18:41.930
<i>Anyway.</i>

18:41.930 --> 18:45.770
That boy, Xiaoyu, seems 
really devoted to his work.

18:45.770 --> 18:48.510
<i>It seems like he's still 
awake watching Sayo-san.</i>

18:48.860 --> 18:50.150
<i>He's not even sleeping?</i>

18:50.150 --> 18:52.730
<i>No, he's outside Sayo-san's door.</i>

18:52.730 --> 18:55.440
<i>He detected me </i>again<i>.</i>

18:55.990 --> 18:58.780
<i>But there are no surveillance 
cameras in here.</i>

19:00.160 --> 19:01.330
I should head home.

19:01.330 --> 19:05.540
<i>I see. So, he wants me to know 
that he's seen through me.</i>

19:07.070 --> 19:10.490
<i>Fine, then. I'll show everyone 
what you really are.</i>

19:11.080 --> 19:15.920
<i>I swear it on my Heilei blood. 
No, in Rozan-sama's name.</i>

19:16.460 --> 19:19.420
Shinjuku
Police Station

19:17.140 --> 19:19.420
Okay, pay close attention.

19:19.420 --> 19:22.760
<b><i>Polka Shinoyama (16)</i></b>

19:19.420 --> 19:22.760
<b><i>Acting together in Shinjuku</i></b>

19:19.420 --> 19:22.760
<b><i>Working with the Shinoyamas?
Left tracks at the "human
knots" crime scene
Lemmings's footprints found</i></b>

19:19.420 --> 19:22.760
<b><i>Calls herself 
"Misaki Sakimiya"
Sakimiya Steel
Dissolved following 
death of Mr. 
and Mrs. Sakimiya</i></b>

19:19.960 --> 19:22.770
This is Polka Shinoyama, age 16.

19:23.350 --> 19:29.640
He was with Girl A, who left footprints 
at the scene of the human knots.

19:30.020 --> 19:31.680
Who drew that picture?

19:32.100 --> 19:33.410
I did.

19:33.410 --> 19:37.000
Polka's mother, Kanon Shinoyama, 
is already deceased.

19:37.000 --> 19:38.850
I'd like to call him a spoiled rich kid,

19:38.850 --> 19:43.180
but there's apparently more to it than that.

19:44.850 --> 19:48.250
Polka Shinoyama is currently away from home.

19:48.250 --> 19:50.660
In addition to visiting Clarissa's bar,

19:50.660 --> 19:55.880
he admitted to having a friendly 
relationship with Takumi Kuruya.

19:55.880 --> 19:59.090
<b><i>Working with the Shinoyamas?</i></b>

19:55.880 --> 19:59.090
And he made another strange remark to Arase.

19:59.380 --> 20:02.310
My parents sold me, so I wouldn't know.

20:03.230 --> 20:08.720
We don't know what he meant by that or 
if it has anything to do with this case.

20:09.000 --> 20:14.290
But, true or false, words people 
blurt out always mean something.

20:14.290 --> 20:19.480
Find out what it is and push, and you 
start to see people's real faces.

20:19.480 --> 20:23.450
<b><i>Working with the Shinoyamas?</i></b>

20:19.480 --> 20:23.450
So, I looked into young Polka's movements.

20:23.740 --> 20:24.910
And guess what?

20:24.910 --> 20:28.150
He tells fortunes in the middle of Shinjuku.

20:24.910 --> 20:31.660
<b><i>Left tracks at the "human knots" crime scene




Lemmings's footprints found</i></b>

20:28.150 --> 20:31.660
That bastard Solitaire would 
get a kick out of this.

20:32.040 --> 20:36.210
Gah! Whoa! Hyah!

20:36.210 --> 20:37.420
What?!

20:41.010 --> 20:42.540
Thank you for your patronage.

20:42.540 --> 20:48.160
My, VR has come a long way during 
my short stint in prison.

20:48.160 --> 20:49.810
It's wonderful.

20:49.810 --> 20:54.480
The march of progress brings innovation 
to the world of illusion as well!

20:54.480 --> 20:56.750
Hey, isn't that Ten'a Sorimura?

21:00.480 --> 21:01.880
Now...

21:02.440 --> 21:06.090
I've got a show to plan in six days.

21:06.400 --> 21:10.020
How will the police use this week?

21:10.020 --> 21:12.290
I can't wait to find out!

21:15.160 --> 21:16.790
Hey! Stop right there!

21:16.790 --> 21:19.650
I'm not a fan of these local measures!

21:21.160 --> 21:25.830
Till we meet again, Akechi-kun! 
You haven't seen the last of me!

21:23.320 --> 21:26.590
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

21:26.590 --> 21:29.390
Fortunes

21:26.590 --> 21:29.390
Good Luck

21:27.550 --> 21:29.390
I haven't worn this in a while.

21:29.820 --> 21:33.350
We reopened quite suddenly.
I wonder if we'll get any customers.

21:33.350 --> 21:36.060
Yeah, we did take a few days off.

21:37.770 --> 21:40.730
Oh, I'm sorry. Readings start this afternoon.

21:40.730 --> 21:41.550
Hm?

21:43.940 --> 21:45.150
Hey there.

21:45.480 --> 21:47.780
Haven't seen you since Clarissa's,

21:48.050 --> 21:49.910
Polka Shinoyama-kun.

21:50.620 --> 21:52.830
H-Hello.

21:54.350 --> 21:56.040
Would you mind

21:56.890 --> 21:58.460
reading <i>my</i> fortune?
